# Response headers for the Cloudflare Workers static assets (wrangler.jsonc serves ./dist; Vite copies
# public/ into it). tests/unit/483-h4-security-headers.unit.mjs pins what is here and why.
#
# Every page: the browser may not guess a type for a file (a user-made file named .js is not run as a
# script), the site may be framed by itself only (a page that frames it to trick a click is refused),
# a link out sends the site's address and no more, and the camera, the microphone and the location
# are off (the app uses none).
#
# Not set, on purpose:
#  - a Content-Security-Policy: it has to be written against a real browser session of the whole app
#    (the PDF worker, pdf.js, Firebase and the jsDelivr fonts), not blind;
#  - a Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: it breaks the Google sign-in popup;
#  - a long Cache-Control for assets/: wrangler.jsonc answers a path that is no file with index.html (a
#    single-page app), and a rule by path would let a browser keep that page for a year under the name of
#    a script that was not there yet. The default (asked about every time, answered 304) is kept.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
